YAML outlines the first document with content: an empty document (a `---` right before another
`---`) is skipped, so the keys of the document after it are listed (the glob view's field
summary reads the same keys). Later documents still aren't outlined.
== args
input/a.yaml
== file input/a.yaml
---
---
name: second
size: 2
---
other: 3
== stdout
input/a.yaml (6 lines)
[L3-L3] name: second
[L4-L4] size: 2
== stderr
== exit 0
